THIRD-PARTY DERIVATIVE WORK - EEZO ORE

  assets/bertieprogression/textures/block/eezo_ore.png

is a derivative of Mojang's bedrock.png. The ore has to be mistaken for bedrock
at a glance, and a texture merely built to bedrock's palette and histogram still
reads as deepslate, so this one starts from the real pattern: about ten per cent
of its pixels are moved to other positions in bedrock's own palette, and a few
dark violet specks are added. texture-work/make_eezo.py performs both steps and
reads the source from the client jar. This file is NOT covered by the public
domain dedication in UNLICENSE; Minecraft assets remain Mojang's, used here under
their terms for modifications of the game.

The two eezo item sprites

  assets/bertieprogression/textures/item/raw_eezo.png
  assets/bertieprogression/textures/item/eezo_ingot.png

are original, drawn pixel by pixel in make_eezo.py, and are covered by the
dedication.

Every other asset here is original.
